        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 86-year-old male patient, admitted on 27/10/2020 due to an acute exacerbation of his known Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD). On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray and arterial blood gas analysis were performed, confirming acute exacerbation without signs of pneumonia. Spirometry supported the known obstructive pattern. Treatment consisted of inhaled short-acting bronchodilators (salbutamol, ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids (prednisolone), and controlled oxygen therapy. The patient responded well, with significant clinical improvement. He was discharged on 28/10/2020 in stable condition. I recommend continuation of optimised inhaler therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
